<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Undoing two transformations</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>A shape is transformed by \(A = {@A@}\), and its image is then transformed by \(B = {@B@}\).</p><p>(a) Find the single matrix that maps the final image back onto the original shape.</p><div>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) A vertex of the final image is \(({@f[1]@},\,{@f[2]@})\). Find the original vertex.</p><div>( [[input:ans2]] , [[input:ans3]] ) [[validation:ans2]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) Going forwards, the single matrix is \(BA = {@BA@}\). To undo two transformations, undo the last one first: \(B^{-1}\) followed by \(A^{-1}\), whose matrix is \(A^{-1}B^{-1} = (BA)^{-1}\).</p><p>\((BA)^{-1} = {@ta@}\), which is also \({@iA@}{@iB@}\).</p><p>(b) \({@ta@}{@fc@} = {@ta.fc@}\), so the original vertex is \(({@to[1]@},\,{@to[2]@})\). Check: \({@BA@}{@ta.fc@} = {@fc@}\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[validate_numeric(ex) := block([sx], sx: ev(ex, simp), if listofvars(ex) = [] and freeof(%i, sx) then "" else "Type a number in each box, not a letter.");
near(L,T) := is(abs(L[1]-T[1]) + abs(L[2]-T[2]) < 0.001);
/* Design: (BA)^-1 = A^-1 B^-1, with matrices. Source: adapted from SMP Book 5 (Metric), Chapter 13, Section 9. det A and det B are 1 or -1, so every inverse and image has integer entries. */
mlist: [[matrix([1,0],[3,-1]),matrix([0,1],[-1,1]),[-6,-4]],[matrix([2,1],[1,0]),matrix([-1,-1],[-1,-2]),[4,6]],[matrix([2,-1],[-1,0]),matrix([1,0],[1,1]),[6,3]],[matrix([1,3],[0,1]),matrix([-1,0],[1,-1]),[0,1]],[matrix([-3,1],[1,0]),matrix([-1,1],[-1,2]),[5,7]],[matrix([-1,-1],[-1,-2]),matrix([0,1],[-1,1]),[3,1]],[matrix([1,0],[3,1]),matrix([2,1],[1,0]),[8,1]],[matrix([0,-1],[1,1]),matrix([-1,0],[-3,-1]),[2,4]],[matrix([1,-1],[-2,1]),matrix([1,-2],[1,-1]),[6,4]],[matrix([-2,-1],[-1,0]),matrix([-1,-1],[1,2]),[6,-8]]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
A: mlist[ix][1]; B: mlist[ix][2]; f: mlist[ix][3];
fc: transpose(matrix(f));
BA: B.A;
ta: invert(BA);
to: list_matrix_entries(ta.fc);
/* diagnostics: undone in the same order, (AB)^-1; BA itself; A^-1 only */
dWO: invert(A.B); dNI: BA; dA: invert(A);
oWO: list_matrix_entries(dWO.fc); oNI: list_matrix_entries(dNI.fc); oA: list_matrix_entries(dA.fc);
tr: invert(A).invert(B);
tw: ta+matrix([1,0],[0,0]); tow: to+[0,1];
iA: invert(A); iB: invert(B);
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
